-- title:
--   Étale extension containing a primitive e-th root of unity
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring in a universe $u$ which is a regular local ring, a domain, and complete with respect to the adic topology of its maximal ideal. Suppose given $\varpi, s \in R$ with $\mathfrak{m}_R = (\varpi, s)$ and $\operatorname{Krull\,dim} R = 2$ (as an element of the extended-integer Krull dimension), and an integer $e > 0$ whose image in $R$ is a unit. The assertion is the existence of a type $R'$ in the same universe $u$, carrying a commutative ring structure for which $R'$ is a regular local ring and a domain, together with an $R$-algebra structure making $R'$ finite and free as an $R$-module, with injective structure map (faithful scalar multiplication), étale over $R$, and complete for the adic topology of $\mathfrak{m}_{R'}$; and of an element $\zeta \in R'$ which is a primitive $e$-th root of unity, such that moreover $\operatorname{Krull\,dim} R' = 2$ and $\mathfrak{m}_{R'}$ is generated by the images of $\varpi$ and $s$ under $R \to R'$.
--
--   This is the root-adjunction step for two-dimensional complete regular local base rings: one enlarges $R$ by a finite étale local extension containing $\mu_e$ without disturbing regularity, dimension, completeness, or the chosen pair of generators of the maximal ideal. It is used in the construction of a Kummer-type presentation $R' \cong R[X]/(X^n - c)$ for cyclic extensions unramified away from a divisor, via [`IsRegularLocalRing.exists_algEquiv_adjoinRoot_X_pow_sub_C_mul_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue`](thm.html#IsRegularLocalRing.exists_algEquiv_adjoinRoot_X_pow_sub_C_mul_of_isCyclic_of_isUnramifiedAt_of_residue).
